    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk100> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our project management methodology combines agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement, ensuring Our can adapt to the client's needs while maintaining a structured approach." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk101> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our past references include working with a regional hospital group on a pilot assistant for medical documentation integrated with a regional hospital group electronic patient record, which demonstrates Our capability to deliver similar projects." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk102> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our also have partnerships with OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider, and Ligeo Santé, a health-IT integrator, which can help address requirements related to data sovereignty, hosting, and integration with existing hospital information systems." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk103> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, Our must acknowledge that some specific requirements, such as the exact details of medical coding for activity reporting, health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), national health identifier (INS), and national framework (SGUR du numérique en santé, Mon Espace Santé, DMP), may require further clarification or specialization beyond Our current context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk104> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given Our available capacity, including a dedicated team with a project director, solution architect, engineers, data scientist, security compliance lead, and additional resources for change management and training, Our are confident in Our ability to deliver a project that meets many of the client's requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk105> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nonetheless, it is crucial to conduct a detailed analysis of all requirements and constraints to ensure Our can fully address each aspect of the client's needs within Our capabilities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk106> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must be accessible from the hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in clinical and administrative activities, fit into existing practices of staff, not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows, let staff access reliable up-to-date information, adapt generated content to the clinical-administrative context, conform generated content to expected quality standards, support medical coding for activity reporting (PMSI, ICD-10) for T2A, take into account dossier context where available, provide response times compatible with daily clinical use, achieve a response time below 2 seconds for common queries, integrate with existing SIH and DPI, support health interoperability standards (HL7, FHIR), national health identifier (INS), and national framework (SGUR du numérique en santé, Mon Espace Santé, DMP)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk107> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can we design an architecture that meets these technical requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk108> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on we company context at Faber IA, I can confirm that we Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, is capable of meeting many of these technical requirements.  our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform supports hospital staff in clinical and administrative activities through our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform intelligent assistance tool, which can be accessed from the hospital staff work environment via API-first design (REST + webhook). our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform is designed to fit into existing practices of staff and avoid introducing a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform provides reliable up-to-date information to staff, adapts generated content to the clinical-administrative context, and conforms generated content to expected quality standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk109> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we health interoperability capabilities include FHIR and HL7 connectors, allowing integration with existing SIH and DPI systems, as well as support for national health identifiers." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk110> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding response times, our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform is designed to achieve a median latency of 1.3 seconds, with common queries having a p95 latency below 2 seconds, meeting the requirement for response times compatible with daily clinical use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk111> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, I must note that while our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform supports many health interoperability standards and frameworks, specific details about supporting national framework (SGUR du numérique en santé, Mon Espace Santé, DMP) would require further review to ensure compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk112> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For medical coding, our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform can be configured to support medical coding for activity reporting, but specifics about PMSI, ICD-10, and T2A would need to be reviewed in more detail to confirm full compatibility." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk113> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, based on the information available within we company context, it appears that we can design an architecture that meets many of these technical requirements, with some areas requiring further review for complete confirmation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk114> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must ensure data sovereignty, protect personal and health data, comply with GDPR, process special category data under GDPR Art. 9, host data exclusively within the European Union, not transfer data outside the European Union, appropriately protect sensitive data with encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant, obtain French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for infrastructure hosting The solution, provide explainable recommendations or suggestions produced by The solution, ensure understanding of elements that led to an output through source grounding and audit trail, comply with regulatory requirements, provide a level of security, and integrate with existing SIH and DPI." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk115> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can we guarantee compliance with these security and regulatory constraints? we can guarantee compliance with several of the mentioned security and regulatory constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk116> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As a company, we holds ISO 27001 certification since 2023, which covers the development, delivery, and operations of we services, including data protection. we also have ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management, which is an extension of ISO 27001." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk117> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, we hold HDS certification through we hosting infrastructure operated on OuraneCloud, ensuring compliance with health-data hosting regulations. we data protection measures include encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256, with key management handled on the European Union infrastructure. we also implement pseudonymisation and data minimisation, along with configurable retention and strict tenant isolation between client corpora." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk118> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) and audit logging of access and system outputs are in place. we process special category data under GDPR Art. 9 for public-sector and health clients, demonstrating we experience in handling sensitive health information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk119> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "OuraneCloud, is SecNumCloud-qualified, ensuring that the infrastructure meets specific security standards. we can ensure data sovereignty as we do not transfer data outside the European Union, and we operations are designed to comply with GDPR requirements. we provide explainable recommendations through we product Atelier, which supports source grounding, audit logs, and traceability. our product Atelier, which supports source grounding, audit logs, and traceability aligns with the need for understanding elements that led to an output and providing explainable suggestions." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk120> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, while we can address many of these constraints directly through we existing certifications, data protection measures, and experience in handling health data, specific compliance such as obtaining French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for new infrastructure or ensuring integration with all existing SIH and DPI systems would need to be confirmed on a case-by-case basis. we current HDS certification is held through OuraneCloud, which covers we processing on this infrastructure." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk121> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In summary, we can guarantee compliance with many of the listed security and regulatory constraints based on we current certifications, data protection measures, and experience in handling sensitive health data within the European Union." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk122> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For specific requirements such as new HDS certification for infrastructure or detailed integration with existing systems, additional confirmation would be necessary." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk123> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires strict compliance with GDPR, processing of special category data under GDPR Art. 9, hosting of data exclusively within the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union, appropriate protection of sensitive data with encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant, French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for infrastructure hosting the solution, explainable recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution, understanding of elements that led to an output through source grounding and audit trail, consistency with HAS guidance on use of AI in healthcare, non-automated clinical or medico-administrative decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional, no requirement for medical device qualification CE marking MDR, implications of use case approaching medical device qualification CE marking MDR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk124> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Can we ensure that we solution complies with all relevant laws and regulations?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk125> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on the company context provided, we can comply with several requirements related to GDPR, data protection, and healthcare regulations. we are a Société par actions simplifiée (SAS) registered in France, which implies familiarity with the European Union regulations, including GDPR. we regulatory compliance is maintained with we Security & Compliance function, specifically monitored for obligations such as GDPR, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and the European Union AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context. we can process special category data under GDPR Art. 9 and ensure that client data is protected, as we retain administrative attestations available, including those required for French public procurement. we intellectual property model involves proprietary software licensed to clients under a subscription/usage model, which implies control over data handling and protection." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk126> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client retains full ownership of The client own documents, ingested corpus, and produced data, and we provide for the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract through we reversibility plan." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk127> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding hosting and data sovereignty, while the company context provided does not explicitly state that data is hosted exclusively within the European Union or that there is no transfer outside the European Union, the company context provided highlights an understanding of regulatory compliance in a health deployment context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk128> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without explicit information on data hosting locations or transfer policies in the company context provided, we cannot guarantee full compliance with these specific requirements based solely on the given information." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk129> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For sensitive data protection, encryption, and pseudonymisation, the company context provided mentions professional liability insurance covering up to 10 million euros per claim and general civil liability cover, indicating a level of responsibility towards data handling but does not explicitly mention encryption or pseudonymisation practices.  we infrastructure must comply with French and the European Union regulations, given Faber IA's infrastructure registration and operation within France." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk130> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The requirement for Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification is noted as part of the healthcare regulatory framework in France, but Faber IA's infrastructureructure holds The requirement for Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk131> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding explainable recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution and understanding elements leading to an output through source grounding and audit trail, explainable recommendations or suggestions produced by the solution and understanding elements leading to an output through source grounding and audit trail are technical requirements that align with principles of transparency and accountability in AI systems. the company context provided indicates an ability to comply with regulatory requirements, including those related to AI, but does not provide specific details on how we solutions achieve explainability or maintain audit trails." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk132> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Consistency with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare is crucial for compliance, and while we monitor EU AI Act requirements, specific adherence to HAS (Haute Autorité de Santé) guidelines would depend on the implementation details of we AI systems, which are not provided in the context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk133> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Non-automated clinical or medico-administrative decisions without explicit validation by a qualified professional are a critical aspect of healthcare regulation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk134> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our system's design must ensure that decisions requiring professional judgment are validated appropriately, but specific mechanisms for validated are not detailed in the company context provided." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk135> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The requirement for no medical device qualification CE marking MDR and the consideration of implications if a use case approaches The requirement for no medical device qualification CE marking MDR are significant. we Legal function is tasked with flagging CE/MDR implications and consequences for liability and positioning when use cases could approach The requirement for no medical device qualification CE marking MDR, indicating an awareness and process for addressing these regulatory boundaries." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk136> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In summary, while the company context provided demonstrates compliance with several aspects of GDPR, data protection, and healthcare regulations, specific guarantees regarding exclusive the European Union hosting, no data transfer outside the European Union, encryption/pseudonymisation practices, HDS certification, explainability, audit trails, and adherence to all detailed requirements would require more explicit confirmations than provided in the company context provided." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk137> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget is estimated at 900,000 euros over 5 years, annual operating costs must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk138> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires a pilot phase followed by progressive rollout." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk139> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimization strategies our can propose? our target gross margin percentage ranges from 25% to 35%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk140> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To estimate our projected margin on this contract, our first need to understand the breakdown of costs within the budget envelope." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk141> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The global budget includes both one-off project costs and recurring run costs, with recurring run costs being approximately 70% of The global budget." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk142> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given that our standard daily rates range from 700 euros for an engineer to 1,300 euros for a project director, our main focus should be on optimizing the use of resources to fit within the client's budget constraints while maintaining our projected margin on this contract." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk143> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "One cost-optimization strategy our can propose is leveraging our financial capacity and flexibility in pricing models." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk144> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Since our funding round provides our with a comfortable cash runway, our might consider competitive pricing for the initial phases of the project, such as a pilot phase, to ensure a strong partnership with the client. competitive pricing could involve allocating experienced but cost-effective resources (like senior engineers instead of project directors) for key tasks." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk145> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Another strategy is to emphasize our ability to work efficiently within the given budget constraints by providing a detailed, phased rollout plan that aligns with the authority's budgetary capacity and operational requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk146> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By demonstrating how our can manage costs effectively through careful resource allocation and project management, our can reassure the client of our commitment to delivering value within the client means." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk147> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, highlighting our cost-efficient tiers and models for recurring costs (such as hosting and inference) could provide further opportunities for optimization." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk148> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For example, selecting a sovereign HDS tier and a European model for inference could offer significant savings on the recurring side without compromising performance or security." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk149> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, without more specific details on how the 900,000 euros is allocated between one-off and recurring costs, it's challenging to provide an exact projected margin. our approach should focus on maximizing efficiency in resource allocation, emphasizing our ability to adapt to the client's budgetary needs, and potentially offering tiered services or phased implementation plans that can be adjusted based on the authority's financial situation and priorities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
